{"id":"mahabharata-12-323","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":323,"title":"त्रयोविंशत्यधिकत्रिशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 323 · Ekata, Dvita and Trita","summary":{"en":"Bhishma tells how, after a great age, the sons of the sage Angiras, Ekata, Dvita and Trita, performed severe austerity for four thousand years. They heard a voice in praise of the lotus-eyed Lord, and one of them, falling and rising by his grace, reached the highest.","kn":"ಮಹಾಕಲ್ಪ ಕಳೆದ ನಂತರ ಅಂಗಿರಸನ ಮಕ್ಕಳು ಏಕತ, ದ್ವಿತ, ತ್ರಿತ ನಾಲ್ಕು ಸಾವಿರ ವರ್ಷ ಕಠಿಣ ತಪಸ್ಸು ಮಾಡಿದ ಕಥೆಯನ್ನು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಪುಂಡರೀಕಾಕ್ಷನ ಸ್ತುತಿಯ ಧ್ವನಿ ಕೇಳಿದರು, ಅವರಲ್ಲಿ ಒಬ್ಬ ಅವನ ಕೃಪೆಯಿಂದ ಬಿದ್ದು ಎದ್ದು ಪರಮ ಗತಿ ಪಡೆದ.","hi":"भीष्म बताते हैं कि महाकल्प बीतने पर अंगिरा के पुत्र एकत, द्वित और त्रित ने चार हजार वर्ष घोर तप किया। उन्होंने कमलनयन भगवान की स्तुति की वाणी सुनी, और उनमें से एक उनकी कृपा से गिरकर उठा और परम गति पाई।","te":"మహాకల్పం గడిచాక అంగిరసుని కొడుకులు ఏకతుడు, ద్వితుడు, త్రితుడు నాలుగు వేల ఏళ్లు కఠిన తపస్సు చేసిన కథను భీష్ముడు చెబుతాడు. పుండరీకాక్షుని స్తుతి ధ్వని విన్నారు, వారిలో ఒకడు ఆయన కృపతో పడి లేచి పరమ గతి పొందాడు.","ta":"ஒரு மகா கல்பம் கடந்த பின் அங்கிரஸின் மகன்கள் ஏகதன், த்விதன், த்ரிதன் நாலாயிரம் ஆண்டுகள் கடுந்தவம் புரிந்த கதையைப் பீஷ்மர் கூறுகிறார். தாமரைக்கண்ணனைப் புகழும் குரலைக் கேட்டனர், அவர்களில் ஒருவன் அவன் அருளால் வீழ்ந்து எழுந்து உயர்ந்த கதி அடைந்தான்.","ml":"ഒരു മഹായുഗത്തിനുശേഷം അംഗിരസ്സിന്റെ പുത്രന്മാരായ ഏകതൻ, ദ്വിതൻ, ത്രിതൻ എന്നിവർ നാലായിരം വർഷം കഠിന തപസ്സു ചെയ്തതെങ്ങനെയെന്ന് ഭീഷ്മർ പറയുന്നു. താമരക്കണ്ണനായ ഭഗവാനെ സ്തുതിക്കുന്ന ഒരു ശബ്ദം അവർ കേട്ടു; അവരിൽ ഒരാൾ അദ്ദേഹത്തിന്റെ കൃപയാൽ വീഴുകയും ഉയരുകയും ചെയ്ത് ഉന്നതത്തിലെത്തി."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.323; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततोऽतीते महाकल्पे उत्पन्नेऽङ्गिरसः सुते ।\nबभूवुर्निर्वृता देवा जाते देवपुरोहिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"After that great cycle had passed and Angiras's son was born, the gods were content when the gods' priest came into being."}},{"n":2,"text":"बृहद्ब्रह्म महच्चेति शब्दाः पर्यायवाचकाः ।\nएभिः समन्वितो राजन्गुणैर्विद्वान्बृहस्पतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Brihad,\" \"Brahma,\" and \"Mahat\" are synonymous words; Brihaspati, the learned, was endowed with these qualities, king."}},{"n":3,"text":"तस्य शिष्यो बभूवाग्र्यो राजोपरिचरो वसुः ।\nअधीतवांस्तदा शास्त्रं सम्यक्चित्रशिखण्डिजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"His foremost pupil was King Vasu Uparichara, who then studied the teaching born of the Chitrashikhandins correctly."}},{"n":4,"text":"स राजा भावितः पूर्वं दैवेन विधिना वसुः ।\nपालयामास पृथिवीं दिवमाखण्डलो यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"That king Vasu, formed beforehand by divine rite, ruled the earth as Indra rules heaven."}},{"n":5,"text":"तस्य यज्ञो महानासीदश्वमेधो महात्मनः ।\nबृहस्पतिरुपाध्यायस्तत्र होता बभूव ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great-souled king performed a great horse sacrifice; Brihaspati, his teacher, served as the chief priest there."}},{"n":6,"text":"प्रजापतिसुताश्चात्र सदस्यास्त्वभवंस्त्रयः ।\nएकतश्च द्वितश्चैव त्रितश्चैव महर्षयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Three sons of Prajapati were members of the assembly there, the great sages Ekata, Dvita, and Trita."}},{"n":7,"text":"धनुषाक्षोऽथ रैभ्यश्च अर्वावसुपरावसू ।\nऋषिर्मेधातिथिश्चैव ताण्ड्यश्चैव महानृषिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Also Dhanushaksha, Raibhya, Arvavasu and Paravasu, the sage Medhatithi, and the great sage Tandya,"}},{"n":8,"text":"ऋषिः शक्तिर्महाभागस्तथा वेदशिराश्च यः ।\nकपिलश्च ऋषिश्रेष्ठः शालिहोत्रपितामहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"the sage Shakti of great fortune, Vedashiras, and Kapila, best of sages, grandfather of Shalihotra,"}},{"n":9,"text":"आद्यः कठस्तैत्तिरिश्च वैशंपायनपूर्वजः ।\nकण्वोऽथ देवहोत्रश्च एते षोडश कीर्तिताः ।\nसंभृताः सर्वसंभारास्तस्मिन्राजन्महाक्रतौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Katha the first, Taittiri, the elder brother of Vaishampayana, Kanva, and Devahotra: these sixteen are named. All the requisites were gathered at that great sacrifice, king."}},{"n":10,"text":"न तत्र पशुघातोऽभूत्स राजैवं स्थितोऽभवत् ।\nअहिंस्रः शुचिरक्षुद्रो निराशीः कर्मसंस्तुतः ।\nआरण्यकपदोद्गीता भागास्तत्रोपकल्पिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"No animal was killed there; the king held to that, nonviolent, pure, not petty, without craving, praised for his rites. Portions were arranged there chanted in the Aranyaka texts."}},{"n":11,"text":"प्रीतस्ततोऽस्य भगवान्देवदेवः पुरातनः ।\nसाक्षात्तं दर्शयामास सोऽदृश्योऽन्येन केनचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the ancient blessed god of gods, pleased with him, showed himself in person to him, though invisible to anyone else."}},{"n":12,"text":"स्वयं भागमुपाघ्राय पुरोडाशं गृहीतवान् ।\nअदृश्येन हृतो भागो देवेन हरिमेधसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"He himself smelled his portion and took the sacrificial cake; the share was taken by the unseen god, of Hari's mind."}},{"n":13,"text":"बृहस्पतिस्ततः क्रुद्धः स्रुवमुद्यम्य वेगितः ।\nआकाशं घ्नन्स्रुवः पातै रोषादश्रूण्यवर्तयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Brihaspati, enraged, raised the ladle and, striking the sky with the ladle's blows, shed tears of anger."}},{"n":14,"text":"उवाच चोपरिचरं मया भागोऽयमुद्यतः ।\nग्राह्यः स्वयं हि देवेन मत्प्रत्यक्षं न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He said to Uparichara, \"This share was held out by me; the god must take it himself in my sight, without doubt."}},{"n":15,"text":"उद्यता यज्ञभागा हि साक्षात्प्राप्ताः सुरैरिह ।\nकिमर्थमिह न प्राप्तो दर्शनं स हरिर्विभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For sacrificial portions held out here are taken by the gods in person; why has Lord Hari not come into view here?\""}},{"n":16,"text":"ततः स तं समुद्धूतं भूमिपालो महान्वसुः ।\nप्रसादयामास मुनिं सदस्यास्ते च सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the great king Vasu and all the assembly members pacified that agitated sage on every side."}},{"n":17,"text":"ऊचुश्चैनमसंभ्रान्ता न रोषं कर्तुमर्हसि ।\nनैष धर्मः कृतयुगे यस्त्वं रोषमचीकृथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Calmly they said to him, \"You should not be angry. This is not the way in the Krita age, that you should show anger."}},{"n":18,"text":"अरोषणो ह्यसौ देवो यस्य भागोऽयमुद्यतः ।\nन स शक्यस्त्वया द्रष्टुमस्माभिर्वा बृहस्पते ।\nयस्य प्रसादं कुरुते स वै तं द्रष्टुमर्हति ॥","meaning":{"en":"For that god, whose portion this is, is free of anger. He cannot be seen by you or by us, Brihaspati; only the one to whom he shows favor can see him.\""}},{"text":"एकतद्वितत्रिता ऊचुः","meaning":{"en":"Ekata, Dvita, and Trita said:"}},{"n":19,"text":"वयं हि ब्रह्मणः पुत्रा मानसाः परिकीर्तिताः ।\nगता निःश्रेयसार्थं हि कदाचिद्दिशमुत्तराम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"We are called Brahma's mind-born sons. Once we went to the northern direction for the sake of the highest good."}},{"n":20,"text":"तप्त्वा वर्षसहस्राणि चत्वारि तप उत्तमम् ।\nएकपादस्थिताः सम्यक्काष्ठभूताः समाहिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having practiced supreme austerity for four thousand years, standing on one foot, concentrated and still as wood,"}},{"n":21,"text":"मेरोरुत्तरभागे तु क्षीरोदस्यानुकूलतः ।\nस देशो यत्र नस्तप्तं तपः परमदारुणम् ।\nकथं पश्येमहि वयं देवं नारायणं त्विति ॥","meaning":{"en":"on the northern side of Meru, near the Ocean of Milk, in the place where we practiced extremely harsh austerity, we wondered how we might see the god Narayana."}},{"n":22,"text":"ततो व्रतस्यावभृथे वागुवाचाशरीरिणी ।\nसुतप्तं वस्तपो विप्राः प्रसन्नेनान्तरात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then at the conclusion of the vow, a bodiless voice spoke: 'Brahmins, your austerity is well done, and I am pleased in heart."}},{"n":23,"text":"यूयं जिज्ञासवो भक्ताः कथं द्रक्ष्यथ तं प्रभुम् ।\nक्षीरोदधेरुत्तरतः श्वेतद्वीपो महाप्रभः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are seekers and devotees; how will you see that lord? North of the Ocean of Milk is the brilliant Shvetadvipa."}},{"n":24,"text":"तत्र नारायणपरा मानवाश्चन्द्रवर्चसः ।\nएकान्तभावोपगतास्ते भक्ताः पुरुषोत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There live men devoted to Narayana, bright as the moon, devotees of the Supreme Person with exclusive devotion."}},{"n":25,"text":"ते सहस्रार्चिषं देवं प्रविशन्ति सनातनम् ।\nअतीन्द्रिया निराहारा अनिष्पन्दाः सुगन्धिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They enter the eternal god of a thousand rays; beyond the senses, without food, motionless and fragrant,"}},{"n":26,"text":"एकान्तिनस्ते पुरुषाः श्वेतद्वीपनिवासिनः ।\nगच्छध्वं तत्र मुनयस्तत्रात्मा मे प्रकाशितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"those men, exclusive in devotion, dwell in Shvetadvipa. Go there, sages; there my Self has been revealed.'"}},{"n":27,"text":"अथ श्रुत्वा वयं सर्वे वाचं तामशरीरिणीम् ।\nयथाख्यातेन मार्गेण तं देशं प्रतिपेदिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having heard that bodiless voice, we all went to that place by the way described."}},{"n":28,"text":"प्राप्य श्वेतं महाद्वीपं तच्चित्तास्तद्दिदृक्षवः ।\nततो नो दृष्टिविषयस्तदा प्रतिहतोऽभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having reached the great white island, with minds fixed on him and desiring to see him, our sight was then blocked."}},{"n":29,"text":"न च पश्याम पुरुषं तत्तेजोहृतदर्शनाः ।\nततो नः प्रादुरभवद्विज्ञानं देवयोगजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"We did not see the Person, our vision stolen by his radiance. Then there arose in us a knowledge born of divine yoga."}},{"n":30,"text":"न किलातप्ततपसा शक्यते द्रष्टुमञ्जसा ।\nततः पुनर्वर्षशतं तप्त्वा तात्कालिकं महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"'He cannot be easily seen by one whose austerity is not heated enough.' So we practiced a great austerity again for a hundred years, suited to that time."}},{"n":31,"text":"व्रतावसाने सुशुभान्नरान्ददृशिरे वयम् ।\nश्वेतांश्चन्द्रप्रतीकाशान्सर्वलक्षणलक्षितान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the end of the vow we saw very auspicious men, white, like the moon, bearing all the marks,"}},{"n":32,"text":"नित्याञ्जलिकृतान्ब्रह्म जपतः प्रागुदङ्मुखान् ।\nमानसो नाम स जपो जप्यते तैर्महात्मभिः ।\nतेनैकाग्रमनस्त्वेन प्रीतो भवति वै हरिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"with hands always folded, facing east and north, muttering the sacred word. That mental recitation is performed by those great souls; by that one-pointedness Hari is pleased."}},{"n":33,"text":"या भवेन्मुनिशार्दूल भाः सूर्यस्य युगक्षये ।\nएकैकस्य प्रभा तादृक्साभवन्मानवस्य ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever the sun's radiance is at the end of an age, tiger among sages, such was the radiance of each one of those men."}},{"n":34,"text":"तेजोनिवासः स द्वीप इति वै मेनिरे वयम् ।\nन तत्राभ्यधिकः कश्चित्सर्वे ते समतेजसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"We thought that island to be the dwelling of splendor; none there was greater, all had equal splendor."}},{"n":35,"text":"अथ सूर्यसहस्रस्य प्रभां युगपदुत्थिताम् ।\nसहसा दृष्टवन्तः स्म पुनरेव बृहस्पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, Brihaspati, we suddenly saw once more the radiance of a thousand suns risen at once."}},{"n":36,"text":"सहिताश्चाभ्यधावन्त ततस्ते मानवा द्रुतम् ।\nकृताञ्जलिपुटा हृष्टा नम इत्येव वादिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those men quickly ran together, hands folded and joyful, saying only, 'Homage!'"}},{"n":37,"text":"ततोऽभिवदतां तेषामश्रौष्म विपुलं ध्वनिम् ।\nबलिः किलोपह्रियते तस्य देवस्य तैर्नरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, as they spoke, we heard a great noise: an offering was being presented by those men to that god."}},{"n":38,"text":"वयं तु तेजसा तस्य सहसा हृतचेतसः ।\nन किंचिदपि पश्यामो हृतदृष्टिबलेन्द्रियाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But we, our minds suddenly stolen by his radiance, saw nothing at all, our sight and senses robbed of strength."}},{"n":39,"text":"एकस्तु शब्दोऽविरतः श्रुतोऽस्माभिरुदीरितः ।\nजितं ते पुण्डरीकाक्ष नमस्ते विश्वभावन ॥","meaning":{"en":"One sound alone we heard, uttered unceasingly: 'You have conquered, lotus-eyed one; homage to you, creator of the universe."}},{"n":40,"text":"नमस्तेऽस्तु हृषीकेश महापुरुषपूर्वज ।\nइति शब्दः श्रुतोऽस्माभिः शिक्षाक्षरसमीरितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Homage to you, Hrishikesha, elder of the great Person.' That sound we heard, uttered in the syllables of phonetic training."}},{"n":41,"text":"एतस्मिन्नन्तरे वायुः सर्वगन्धवहः शुचिः ।\nदिव्यान्युवाह पुष्पाणि कर्मण्याश्चौषधीस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Meanwhile a pure wind carrying every fragrance bore divine flowers and herbs useful for rites."}},{"n":42,"text":"तैरिष्टः पञ्चकालज्ञैर्हरिरेकान्तिभिर्नरैः ।\nनूनं तत्रागतो देवो यथा तैर्वागुदीरिता ।\nवयं त्वेनं न पश्यामो मोहितास्तस्य मायया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hari had surely been worshiped by those exclusive devotees, knowers of the five times; surely the god came there, as their voice proclaimed. But we did not see him, bewildered by his illusion."}},{"n":43,"text":"मारुते संनिवृत्ते च बलौ च प्रतिपादिते ।\nचिन्ताव्याकुलितात्मानो जाताः स्मोऽङ्गिरसां वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the wind had stopped and the offering was presented, we were agitated in mind with worry, best of the Angirasas."}},{"n":44,"text":"मानवानां सहस्रेषु तेषु वै शुद्धयोनिषु ।\nअस्मान्न कश्चिन्मनसा चक्षुषा वाप्यपूजयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Among those thousands of men of pure birth, none honored us in mind or with a glance."}},{"n":45,"text":"तेऽपि स्वस्था मुनिगणा एकभावमनुव्रताः ।\nनास्मासु दधिरे भावं ब्रह्मभावमनुष्ठिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those groups of sages, composed and following one single devotion, fixed in the state of Brahman, gave us no regard."}},{"n":46,"text":"ततोऽस्मान्सुपरिश्रान्तांस्तपसा चापि कर्शितान् ।\nउवाच खस्थं किमपि भूतं तत्राशरीरकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then to us, quite exhausted and wasted by austerity, some bodiless being in the sky spoke:"}},{"n":47,"text":"दृष्टा वः पुरुषाः श्वेताः सर्वेन्द्रियविवर्जिताः ।\nदृष्टो भवति देवेश एभिर्दृष्टैर्द्विजोत्तमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"'You have seen the white men devoid of all senses; seeing them, the lord of gods is seen, best of twice-born."}},{"n":48,"text":"गच्छध्वं मुनयः सर्वे यथागतमितोऽचिरात् ।\nन स शक्यो अभक्तेन द्रष्टुं देवः कथंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Go, sages, all of you, back as you came, at once. That god cannot be seen by one without devotion."}},{"n":49,"text":"कामं कालेन महता एकान्तित्वं समागतैः ।\nशक्यो द्रष्टुं स भगवान्प्रभामण्डलदुर्दृशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Over a great time, those who have attained exclusive devotion can, if they wish, see that blessed one, hard to look at for his orb of radiance."}},{"n":50,"text":"महत्कार्यं तु कर्तव्यं युष्माभिर्द्विजसत्तमाः ।\nइतः कृतयुगेऽतीते विपर्यासं गतेऽपि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"But a great task must be done by you, best of the twice-born. When the Krita age has passed hence and turned into reversal,"}},{"n":51,"text":"वैवस्वतेऽन्तरे विप्राः प्राप्ते त्रेतायुगे ततः ।\nसुराणां कार्यसिद्ध्यर्थं सहाया वै भविष्यथ ॥","meaning":{"en":"in the interval of Vaivasvata, brahmins, when the Treta age arrives, you will be helpers for the accomplishment of the gods' purpose.'"}},{"n":52,"text":"ततस्तदद्भुतं वाक्यं निशम्यैवं स्म सोमप ।\nतस्य प्रसादात्प्राप्ताः स्मो देशमीप्सितमञ्जसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that wondrous word, Soma-drinker, by his grace we reached the place we wished."}},{"n":53,"text":"एवं सुतपसा चैव हव्यकव्यैस्तथैव च ।\nदेवोऽस्माभिर्न दृष्टः स कथं त्वं द्रष्टुमर्हसि ।\nनारायणो महद्भूतं विश्वसृग्घव्यकव्यभुक् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus, though we practiced such austerity and offered oblations to gods and ancestors, we did not see that god. How can you expect to see him? Narayana is a great being, creator of the universe, enjoyer of offerings to gods and ancestors.\""}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":54,"text":"एवमेकतवाक्येन द्वितत्रितमतेन च ।\nअनुनीतः सदस्यैश्च बृहस्पतिरुदारधीः ।\nसमानीय ततो यज्ञं दैवतं समपूजयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, appeased by the word of Ekata and the view of Dvita and Trita and by the assembly members, the noble-minded Brihaspati gathered the sacrifice and worshiped the god."}},{"n":55,"text":"समाप्तयज्ञो राजापि प्रजाः पालितवान्वसुः ।\nब्रह्मशापाद्दिवो भ्रष्टः प्रविवेश महीं ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"King Vasu, when the sacrifice was complete, protected his subjects; by a brahmin's curse he fell from heaven and entered the earth."}},{"n":56,"text":"अन्तर्भूमिगतश्चैव सततं धर्मवत्सलः ।\nनारायणपरो भूत्वा नारायणपदं जगौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Constantly devoted to dharma even in the earth, devoted to Narayana, he sang the name of Narayana's state."}},{"n":57,"text":"तस्यैव च प्रसादेन पुनरेवोत्थितस्तु सः ।\nमहीतलाद्गतः स्थानं ब्रह्मणः समनन्तरम् ।\nपरां गतिमनुप्राप्त इति नैष्ठिकमञ्जसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"By that same grace he rose up again; going from the surface of the earth, he reached the place next to Brahma's, and so attained the highest goal, a fixed one for the devoted."}}]}]}